@startuml UC-USER-ACCOUNT-REACTIVATE
' UC-32.3 - Reactivate User Account | semantic key: UC-USER-ACCOUNT-REACTIVATE
' Source: data/use_cases/system-administration/UC-USER-ACCOUNT-REACTIVATE.yml
' Business Rules: BR-SYSADMIN-USER-ACCOUNT, BR-AUDIT-EVENT-COMPLETENESS
' Trace comments ' [ref] name the YAML element behind the next action.
' No title: the Word caption supplies it.
' One Activity Final shared by all paths (team decision 2026-10-06; UML allows one or several). It
' is reached after the account is reactivated and the audit event recorded (postconditions met) or
' with the account not reactivated (AF-01: stays suspended; EX-01: deleted before confirmation).
' EX-01 is checked after the confirmation because the YAML places the deletion before the
' reactivation is confirmed. AF-01.1 is an explicit System step of the YAML, so it is kept as an action.
' Layout (2026-10-06): the decision "Confirm reactivation?" is drawn in the System lane, where the
' System waits for the System Administrator's answer; the guards name the System Administrator's
' choice. In the System Administrator lane its merge forced a detour across the lanes. The final
' stays in the System lane.
!include ../../_shared/activity-style.puml
|ADM| $lane_title("System Administrator")
|SYS| $lane_title("System")

|ADM|
start
' [NF1, TRIGGER, BR-SYSADMIN-USER-ACCOUNT]
:Select suspended User account
and request reactivation;
|SYS|
' [NF2]
:Display account status
and request confirmation;
if ($question("Confirm reactivation?")) then ($guard_left("[confirm]"))
  |ADM|
  ' [NF3]
  :Confirm reactivation;
  |SYS|
  if ($question_x("Account still exists?")) then ($guard_left("[exists]"))
    ' [NF4, POST1, POST2, BR-AUDIT-EVENT-COMPLETENESS, OTHER]
    :Reactivate account and
    record audit event;
  else ($guard_right("[deleted", "— EX-01]"))
    ' [EX-01, GUIDE-7.3]
    :Reject reactivation;
  endif
else ($guard_right("[cancel", "— AF-01]"))
  |SYS|
  ' [AF-01.1]
  :Leave account suspended;
endif
|SYS|
stop
@enduml
